"instead, they take the background of the system tray area.\n"
"Note: after changing this option you need to restart KNetLoad."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 78
#: rc.cpp:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "Active"
msgstr "Gweithredol"

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 80
#: rc.cpp:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enable or disable the network load monitor.\n"
"This option is provided when the CPU is doing expensive work, or when the "
"remote interface is not available (for example, if the network is down), to "
"avoid useless SNMP requests."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 86
#: rc.cpp:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the type of the interface to monitor. KNetLoad 3 supports two "
"types of interfaces: local and SNMP remote.\n"
"This setting determines which settings will be applied in the corresponding "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 89
#: rc.cpp:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Local Interface"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 91
#: rc.cpp:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A local interface is an interface present in the machine where KNetLoad is "
"running.\n"
"Load data about this interface will be requested from the operating system, "
"depending on how it is supported in KNetLoad."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 94
#: rc.cpp:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remote (SNMP) Interface"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 96
#: rc.cpp:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remote interfaces are accessed using the net-snmp library to connect to the "
"SNMP server.\n"
"Example of uses of remote SNMP interfaces are routers, printers, "
"miscellaneous servers, switches..."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 102
#: rc.cpp:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "Update interval (in msecs)"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 103
#: rc.cpp:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The interval between two reads of the interface's network load in "
"milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 107
#: rc.cpp:257
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input scale"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 109
#: rc.cpp:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The maximum value for the input graph.\n"
"If this value is 0, it will take the &quot;Output scale&quot; value."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 113
#: rc.cpp:264
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scale output"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 116
#: rc.cpp:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The maximum value for the output graph.\n"
"If this value is 0 and the interface is a remote one, the value will be "
"retrieved from the SNMP server's statistics.\n"
"If this value is 0 and the interface is a local one, the graphs are disabled."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 122
#: rc.cpp:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface name"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 124
#: rc.cpp:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the interface, such as eth0, ppp0 or lo.\n"
"This is dependant on the operating system you are running."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 130
#: rc.cpp:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "SNMP Server"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 131
#: rc.cpp:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "Server's IP or hostname to monitor the interface of."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 134
#: rc.cpp:285
#, no-c-format
msgid "Community string"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 136
#: rc.cpp:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Community's name to use to read the server's interface statistics.\n"
"This is something like a password, but in many cases is simply the 'public' "
"literal (without quotes)."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 140
#: rc.cpp:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface's index"
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file knetload.kcfg line 143
#: rc.cpp:295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Index of the interface to monitor.\n"
"In SNMP management, the interfaces are not recognized by names, but by their "
"index.\n"
"Actually, there is also a name attribute which allows to search by name the "
"interfaces, but at the moment you should fill the interface's index to "
"monitor it."
msgstr ""

